PATCH 178: faithful 16-bit reconstruction of the MGAVIDEO run-length MASK fill FUN_0000_2595
(supersedes patch 174's body).  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_mga_image.bin 0x2595-0x25d0.

Patch 174 rebased the ES buffer base correctly but modelled di/cx as 32-bit host pointers + an `int`
counter seeded to -0x600 (= 0xfa00 read as a SIGNED 16-bit).  The asm's `sub cx,bx ; jcxz` is 16-bit:
cx is the total byte budget and di/cx WRAP inside the 64KB es segment, so the scan is intrinsically
bounded to the buffer.  The 32-bit model never wrapped and the counter never reached 0 -> the cursor
ran off the end of g_mem -> SIGSEGV (gdb-confirmed: pcVar9 reached g_mem+0x184C00, past g_mem, with a
valid es_seg=0x55ac buffer of real RLE mask data).

Reconstructed as a direct transliteration with uint16_t di/cx: NEGATIVE control byte = one scasb
candidate (cx-=|ctl|+1, replace es:[di] if ==al); NON-NEGATIVE = a run of (ctl+1) bytes, repnz scasb
replacing every al match with ah.  al=(byte)param_1, ah=(byte)(param_1>>8).

Reached only on the ACCEPT mission cascade (the in-mission display-list PAINT via 47e0), unreached by
the 19 verify flows -> behaviour-neutral.  Sources stay pristine; fist_mga.c via build/.

